{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":279860,"duration_api_ms":277584,"num_turns":20,"result":"Perfect! The workflow knowledge report has been generated successfully. Here is the complete file content:\n\n---\n\n# 1000Genome Workflow Knowledge Report\n\n**Workflow Name:** 1000genome\n**Analysis Tool:** Claude (Haiku 4.5)\n**Analysis Date:** 2026-03-11\n**Scope:** Static code analysis only\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThe 1000Genome workflow analyzes genetic variation data from the 1000 Genomes Project. It processes VCF (Variant Call Format) files for each chromosome, extracts per-individual mutation data, filters mutations by SIFT scores, and computes mutation overlap statistics across population groups. The workflow is data-intensive, with parallelization across chromosomes and configurable within-chromosome parallelism.\n\n---\n\n## Section 1: Stages and Tasks\n\n### Stage 1: Data Extraction and Parsing (Individuals Processing)\n\n**Task: `individuals`**\n- **Purpose:** Extract SNP variants from VCF files and create per-individual output records\n- **Inputs:** VCF file `ALL.chrX.250000.vcf` (250,000 lines per chromosome), Columns mapping file `columns.txt`\n- **Outputs:** Tar archive `chrXn-{counter}-{stop}.tar.gz` (contains per-individual mutation files)\n- **Processing Logic:** Reads VCF file in chunks, filters header lines, applies allele frequency threshold, creates per-individual files, compresses output\n- **Parallelism:** One job per chromosome (or multiple jobs if chunked)\n\n### Stage 1b: Individuals Merge\n\n**Task: `individuals_merge`**\n- **Purpose:** Consolidate per-individual results from multiple individuals jobs (when chunked)\n- **Inputs:** Multiple tar archives `chrXn-{counter1}-{stop1}.tar.gz`, etc.\n- **Outputs:** Merged tar archive `chrXn.tar.gz`\n- **Processing Logic:** Extracts all input tar archives, aggregates files by name, re-compresses merged directory\n- **Trigger:** Only created if `ind_jobs > 1`\n\n### Stage 2: Variant Effect Filtering (SIFT Scoring)\n\n**Task: `sifting`**\n- **Purpose:** Filter variants by SIFT (Sorting Intolerant From Tolerant) scores\n- **Inputs:** VEP-annotated VCF file `ALL.chrX.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf`\n- **Outputs:** Text file `sifted.SIFT.chrX.txt`\n- **Processing Logic:** Grep-filters lines with SIFT scores and \"rs\" prefix, extracts variant metadata from VCF INFO field\n- **Output Format:** Space-delimited text (line number, rs number, ENSG ID, SIFT prediction, phenotype)\n\n### Stage 3: Mutation Overlap Analysis\n\n**Task: `mutation_overlap`**\n- **Purpose:** Measure mutation overlap (pairwise similarity) across individuals within a population\n- **Inputs:** Individuals tar archive `chrXn.tar.gz`, SIFT file, population file, columns mapping\n- **Outputs:** Tar archive `chrX-{population_id}.tar.gz`, PNG plots, data files\n- **Processing Logic:** Extracts individuals, reads population IDs, computes pairwise overlap, generates heatmap visualizations\n\n### Stage 4: Mutation Frequency Analysis\n\n**Task: `frequency`**\n- **Purpose:** Estimate mutation frequency statistics via random sampling\n- **Inputs:** Same as mutation_overlap\n- **Outputs:** Tar archive `chrX-{population_id}-freq.tar.gz`, PNG plots, data files\n- **Statistical Method:** Monte Carlo sampling (n_indiv=52 individuals, n_runs=1000 iterations) to establish null distribution\n\n---\n\n## Section 2: Data Objects Registry\n\n### Input Data Objects\n\n| Object Name | Format | Size Estimate | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ALL.chrX.250000.vcf` | VCF (text) | 6-10 GB | SNP variants per chromosome |\n| `ALL.chrX.phase3_*.annotation.vcf` | VEP-annotated VCF | 5-8 GB | Variant effect predictions (SIFT scores) |\n| `columns.txt` | Text | ~100 KB | Individual IDs mapping |\n| `{population_id}` | Text | 1-10 KB | Population-specific individual IDs |\n| `data.csv` | CSV | <1 KB | Metadata: VCF file, row count, VEP file reference |\n\n### Intermediate Data Objects\n\n| Object Name | Format | Produced By | Consumed By | Size |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `chrXn-{counter}-{stop}.tar.gz` | Tar+gzip | Individuals | Individuals_Merge | 500 MB - 2 GB |\n| `chrXn.tar.gz` | Tar+gzip | Individuals_Merge | Mutation_Overlap, Frequency | 2-5 GB |\n| `sifted.SIFT.chrX.txt` | Text | Sifting | Mutation_Overlap, Frequency | 10-50 MB |\n\n### Output Data Objects\n\n| Object Name | Format | Produced By | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `chrX-{population_id}.tar.gz` | Tar+gzip | Mutation_Overlap | Mutation overlap results + plots |\n| `chrX-{population_id}-freq.tar.gz` | Tar+gzip | Frequency | Frequency analysis results + plots |\n| `*.txt` (in output_no_sift/) | Text | Mutation_Overlap, Frequency | Mutation counts, individual lists, gene pair statistics |\n| `*.png` (in plots_no_sift/) | PNG image | Mutation_Overlap, Frequency | Heatmaps, distributions, scatter plots |\n\n---\n\n## Section 3: Producer-Consumer Dependencies\n\n### Data Flow Edges\n\nVCF Files → [Individuals] → tar archives → [Individuals_Merge] → chrXn.tar.gz ↘\n                                                                                ├→ [Mutation_Overlap] → Results\nAnnotated VCF → [Sifting] → sifted.SIFT.chrX.txt ──────────────────────────→ ├→ [Frequency] → Results\n\nPopulation Files → [Mutation_Overlap], [Frequency]\n\n### Critical Path Analysis\n\n**Critical Data Bottleneck:** `chrXn.tar.gz` (merged individuals result)\n- Required by both Mutation_Overlap and Frequency\n- Size: 2-5 GB per chromosome\n- Serialization/deserialization overhead (tar.gz compress/decompress)\n\n**Parallelism Opportunities:**\n1. Chromosome-level: All chromosomes processed independently (10 chromosomes)\n2. Within-chromosome: Individuals jobs can be chunked (if ind_jobs > 1)\n3. Population-level: Each (chromosome, population) pair produces independent analysis\n4. Cross-analysis: Mutation_Overlap and Frequency both independent; sifting independent from individuals\n\n---\n\n## Section 4: Workflow Structure and Pattern\n\n### High-Level Pattern\n\n**Pattern Type:** Multi-stage DAG with parallel fan-out and convergence\n\n### Control Flow\n\n1. **Initialization:** Load metadata (data.csv, population files)\n2. **Per Chromosome:** Individuals task (possibly chunked) → Merge (if chunked), Sifting task (parallel)\n3. **Per Population:** Launch mutation_overlap and frequency jobs per (chromosome, population) pair\n4. **Termination:** All output staged to local storage\n\n### Iteration Behavior\n\n- **Chromosome Iteration:** Implicit; data.csv lists 10 chromosomes (chr1-chr10)\n- **Population Iteration:** Explicit loop over 7 populations (ALL, EUR, EAS, AFR, AMR, SAS, GBR)\n- **Chunked Iteration:** Configurable via `-i` parameter; default: 1 individual job per chromosome\n\n### Dependency Management\n\n**Pegasus `infer_dependencies=True`:** Automatically infers task dependencies from input/output file declarations; no explicit dependency edges needed.\n\n---\n\n## Section 5: I/O Behavioral Hints\n\n### I/O Patterns Observed\n\n1. **Large-File Streaming:** VCF files (250k lines, 6-10 GB) read entirely into memory; memory overhead potential\n2. **Per-Individual Output Explosion:** 2,504 separate files created; high metadata overhead; filesystem inode pressure risk\n3. **Serialization Overhead:** Tar+gzip compression after file creation; CPU/storage delay; [ASSUMPTION] tar format enables directory structure preservation\n4. **Partial/Selective Reads:** SIFT filtering via grep (optimized); avoids full file parsing\n5. **Columnar Access Patterns:** Column-based VCF parsing; repeated string splitting (O(n) per line); no caching\n6. **Plot Generation:** In-memory matplotlib heatmaps; memory overhead proportional to individual/variant count\n7. **Temporary Directories:** Individuals task cleans up; analysis tasks leave output (implicit cleanup assumption)\n8. **Data Reuse:** Both Mutation_Overlap and Frequency read same inputs; no inter-task caching; independent decompression\n\n### Memory and Disk Patterns\n\n| Task | Input Memory | Output Disk | Bottleneck |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Individuals | 6-10 GB (VCF) | 2-5 GB (tar) | RAM (full VCF in memory) |\n| Individuals_Merge | ~500 MB (per chunk) | 2-5 GB (tar) | Disk I/O |\n| Sifting | 5-8 GB (VCF) | 10-50 MB | Disk I/O (grep subprocess) |\n| Mutation_Overlap | ~2-5 GB (extracted) | 100-500 MB | Memory (heatmap matrix) |\n| Frequency | ~2-5 GB (extracted) | 100-500 MB | Memory (random sampling, matrices) |\n\n### Performance Profile (from README)\n\n- Individuals: **81.85%** of total time (critical path)\n- Frequency: **10.68%**\n- Individuals_Merge: **3.58%**\n- Mutation_Overlap: **3.35%**\n\n---\n\n## Section 6: Workflow Metadata and Configuration\n\n### Execution Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Default | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `-D, --dataset` | string | `20130502` | Data folder version |\n| `-f, --datafile` | string | `data.csv` | Input metadata file |\n| `-i, --individuals-jobs` | int | 1 | Parallelism factor (chunk size) |\n| `-e, --execution-site` | string | `local` | Backend: `local` (HTCondor) or `cori` (NERSC) |\n| `-p, --src-path` | string | (auto) | Source directory |\n| `-b, --bash-jobs` | bool | False | Use bash vs Python |\n| `-d, --decaf` | bool | False | In-memory data staging |\n| `-c, --pmc` | bool | False | MPI-based job clustering |\n\n### Populations Supported\n\nALL, EUR, EAS, AFR, AMR, SAS, GBR (7 total)\n\n### Deployment Modes\n\n1. **Local (HTCondor):** Default\n2. **NERSC (Cori):** `--execution-site cori`; uses SLURM via Pegasus/Bosco\n\n---\n\n## Section 7: Internal Consistency and Key Assumptions\n\n### Key Assumptions\n\n1. **[ASSUMPTION]** File Layout: `data/{dataset}/` and `data/populations/` directory structure\n2. **[ASSUMPTION]** VCF Format: Standard VCF with 2504 individual columns (positions 9+)\n3. **[ASSUMPTION]** Allele Frequency Field: In VCF INFO column (field 8); extracted as 8th element post-split\n4. **[ASSUMPTION]** SIFT Annotations: VEP-annotated VCF with pipe-delimited INFO; fields contain ENSG ID, SIFT, phenotype\n5. **[ASSUMPTION]** Population Files: Space/newline-delimited individual IDs; intersection with columns.txt defines sample set\n6. **[ASSUMPTION]** Chromosome Naming: `chr1`, `chr2`, ..., `chr22` convention\n7. **[ASSUMPTION]** Row Count Divisibility: `ind_jobs` must evenly divide total rows; enforced at generation time\n\n### Validation Points\n\n- `ind_jobs` divides row count: daxgen.py line 376-377 (workflow generation)\n- Population files readable: daxgen.py line 84-86 (workflow generation)\n- Column file exists: ReplicaCatalog (runtime)\n- VCF files readable: ReplicaCatalog (runtime)\n\n### Known Constraints\n\n- Individuals: Missing AF values cause ValueError → line skipped (silent)\n- Sifting: Grep subprocess stderr not captured (potential silent failures)\n- Analysis: Empty population intersections not validated (could produce empty output)\n\n---\n\n## Section 8: Summary of Workflow Logic\n\n### Three-Phase Execution Model\n\n**Phase 1: Data Extraction**\n- Input: Raw VCF + population metadata\n- Process: Per-chromosome, per-individual extraction\n- Output: Serialized individual mutation sets (tar.gz)\n- Parallelism: Across chromosomes + within-chromosome chunking\n\n**Phase 2: Variant Filtering**\n- Input: Annotated VCF with SIFT scores\n- Process: Grep-based filtering + SIFT record parsing\n- Output: SIFT score index (one file per chromosome)\n- Parallelism: Across chromosomes\n\n**Phase 3: Analysis**\n- Input: Individual mutations + SIFT annotations + population definitions\n- Processes:\n  - Mutation_Overlap: Pairwise similarity + heatmap visualization\n  - Frequency: Monte Carlo null distribution via random sampling\n- Output: Results matrices, statistics, PNG plots\n- Parallelism: Across (chromosome, population) pairs\n\n### Data-Driven Scalability\n\n- **Chromosomes:** 10 → 10× individuals + sifting tasks\n- **Individuals:** 2,504 per chromosome; per-individual files contained via tar\n- **Populations:** 7 defined; 10 chr × 7 pop × 2 tasks = 140 analysis jobs\n- **Parallelism:** ind_jobs scaling from 1 → 250 increases job count 25× (2500 individuals + 250 merge tasks)\n\n---\n\n## Glossary\n\n- **VCF:** Variant Call Format; standard format for genetic variants\n- **SNP:** Single Nucleotide Polymorphism; common genetic variation\n- **SIFT:** Sorting Intolerant From Tolerant; amino acid substitution effect predictor\n- **VEP:** Variant Effect Predictor; variant annotation tool\n- **Allele Frequency (AF):** Variant prevalence in population [0, 1]\n- **Individual/Sample:** Sequenced person (2504 total in 1000 Genomes)\n- **Population Group:** Super-population aggregation (ALL, EUR, EAS, AFR, AMR, SAS, GBR)\n- **DAG:** Directed Acyclic Graph; Pegasus execution model\n- **Stage-out:** Output data transfer from compute to storage\n\n---\n\nSTATUS: success | OUTPUT: /home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_knowledge/1000genome-knowledge-claude-trial1.md","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"eab7fbb6-f135-42ee-963a-aeca106a13a0","total_cost_usd":0.27132890000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":171,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56724,"cache_read_input_tokens":635229,"output_tokens":27346,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56724,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":171,"outputTokens":27346,"cacheReadInputTokens":635229,"cacheCreationInputTokens":56724,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.27132890000000004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"50524286-98a0-46ee-b53f-b4cce8aa23d2"}
